```bash
${package} --help
```

## Development

```bash
git clone <repository-url>
cd ${name}
make dev      # Install in development mode with all dependencies
make test     # Run tests
make lint     # Run linter
make format   # Format code
make docs     # Build HTML documentation
make docs-pdf # Build a single PDF of the docs (needs a LaTeX toolchain)
```

`make docs-pdf` produces `docs/_build/latex/${package}.pdf`. It needs a system
LaTeX toolchain on `PATH` — `xelatex`, `latexmk`, and `makeindex` (install
[TeX Live](https://www.tug.org/texlive/) or, on Windows,
[MiKTeX](https://miktex.org/)). The toolchain is **not** pip-installable and is
optional: the target fails fast with a clear message if `latexmk` is missing.
Read the Docs builds and hosts the PDF automatically (its image already has the
toolchain), so no local install is required just to publish a PDF.

